    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d206-a1">

                <pb facs="0316" n="218" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg218"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure—Translation<anchor n="77"
                            xml:id="d206-f1"/>]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Argentine Minister of Foreign Affairs and
                        Worship</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pueyrredon</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-18"><hi rendition="#italic">May 18,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have the honor to address Your
                    Excellency and to inform you that the Government of Guatemala has written to the
                    Ministry a note, of which I enclose an authenticated copy, giving notice that
                    the Government of Guatemala, finding it inconvenient to <pb facs="0317" n="219"
                        xml:id="pg219"/> continue a party to the convention relative to trade marks,
                    concluded at the Fourth International Conference of American States which met at
                    this capital in 1910, sees fit to denounce it as it does by means of the said
                    note.</p>
                <p>Therefore, in accordance with the stipulation in article 19 of the said
                    convention, I forward that document to Your Excellency for the notice and
                    information of your Government.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Pueyrredon</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
